From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: smit1237 <smit1237@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 01:14:22 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 17/30] portal: check for a newer rnsd and show it in the web
 UI

Adds a notify-only update checker. rnsbox_portal.updatecheck queries PyPI for
the latest Reticulum "rns" (rnsd) release, compares it to the installed version
(from package metadata, RNS._version fallback), and records the result in
/var/lib/rnsbox/update.json. It never touches the installed package or any user
config, and is offline-safe -- check() never raises and keeps the last known
result.

S84cron runs the checker daily at 05:00 and once, best-effort, ~30s after boot
(gated on /run/clock-synced); the periodic check is toggleable via
/etc/rnsbox/cron.conf (update_check=yes|no). The portal shows the installed rnsd
version plus an "update available" badge on the Reticulum tab and the Dashboard,
with a "Check now" button and an auto-check toggle. store.py's cron.conf helpers
were generalized to whole-dict read/write so update_check and rnsd_restart_days
no longer clobber each other. Upgrading rnsd itself is out of scope (that means
reflashing the image) -- this only notifies.
